; The documented rule shape: measure, then hand dune the corrected file to
; diff. No (universe), no no-infer copy: an unchanged exe and baseline is a
; cache hit, and diff? tolerates the corrected file's absence on a pass.
; (--quick -f alloc keeps the session fast and its verdicts exact; the
; shipped template is flagless.)

(rule
 (alias bench)
 (locks %{project_root}/bench)
 (action
  (progn
   (run %{exe:bench.exe} --quick -f alloc)
   (diff? fixture.thumper fixture.thumper.corrected))))
